  = help: the plot maps `abs(wage)` to `y`, so it must come to a number on the frame of every layer

let w = dataset(wages)
let d = frame(educ = [1, 2], wage = ["a", "b"])
w.plot(x: educ, y: wage * 2).points(data: d)
error[Z0215]: `*` does not apply to text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:43
  |
3 | w.plot(x: educ, y: wage * 2).points(data: d)
  |                              ------ this layer draws `wage * 2`, which the plot maps to `y`
  |                                           ^ `wage * 2` cannot be computed on this frame
  |
  = help: `join` puts texts together and `format` builds text from values (release 0.5.0); a number in text converts with `to(x, Float)`

